> The default green explanation container under revealed questions will be replaced by the direct options highlight + a dedicated AI Tutor button + a clean correct answer indicator. This streamlines the interface, reduces layout clutter, and encourages AI Tutor engagement.
const DIFF_COLORS = { Easy: '#10b981', Medium: '#f59e0b', Hard: '#ef4444' };
- **Problem**: Solved questions were saved to the database upon clicking "Mark as Solved", but when refreshing the page or navigating back, the solved state (green border & "✓ Solved" label) was lost because the page never loaded the user's progress history.
- **Root Cause**: The `.site-header` had `z-index: 40` but did not have a CSS position property set, meaning the `z-index` was ignored. The sticky sub-header `.sticky-prep-header` in [AptitudePrep.jsx](file:///d:/job/client/src/pages/Preparation/AptitudePrep.jsx) had `z-index: 80`, causing it to overlap the dropdowns.
- **Fixed & Uniform Card Height**: Adjusted flex stretching rules so cards in the same row are guaranteed to have identical heights regardless of topic count variation.
- Modified [global.css](file:///d:/job/client/src/styles/global.css): Added `position: relative` and raised `z-index` of `.site-header` to `150`.
- **Generic "View More Topics" Toggle**: Added a custom toggle button to any subcategories exceeding 4 topics. The button's background and text utilize the parent subject's theme color, expanding the view to show all topics in a responsive 2-column grid.
- Modified [preparationController.js](file:///D:/job/server/controllers/preparationController.js): Updated the `getUserProgress` handler to return the full `solvedQuestions` history.
- Modified [DSAPrep.jsx](file:///D:/job/client/src/pages/Preparation/DSAPrep.jsx):
- **Database Models**: Created Mongoose models `PrepCategory.js` (representing the Category -> Sub Category -> Topic tree) and `PrepCompany.js` (storing corporate recruiter tags).
- **Problem**: Preparation layouts spanned the full 100% width of the screen, pushing the sidebar to the extreme left edge and misaligning the content body from the global site header (which is centered at `1200px` max-width).
- **Dynamic API Route**: Added public `GET /api/preparation/structure` to fetch active categories, subcategories, topics, and companies for the student-facing dashboard.
- Modified [PrepLayout.jsx](file:///d:/job/client/src/components/Preparation/PrepLayout.jsx): Added `max-width: 1200px` and `margin: 0 auto` to the `.hub-outer-container`.
- Now, both the Preparation Hub landing page (`/preparation`) and all category-level pages (such as `/preparation/aptitude?category=Data%20Interpretation`) align perfectly with the centered `1200px` main site header.
- Implemented full CRUD endpoints for Category Tree (add/edit/delete/reorder/toggle) and Company Mappings (add/edit/delete/reorder/toggle) in `preparationController.js` protected by `adminAuth` middleware.
- **Excel Spreadsheet Parser**: Installed `xlsx` on the server to parse uploaded Excel sheets, validate columns, and bulk insert questions while preventing duplicates.
- Modified [DSAQuestion.js](file:///D:/job/server/models/DSAQuestion.js): Added optional fields `solutionCodeCpp`, `solutionCodeJava`, and `solutionCodePython` to the schema.
- **Root Cause**: The min/max distribution range pins inside the salary range bar in [SalarySearch.jsx](file:///d:/job/client/src/pages/SalarySearch.jsx) were absolute-positioned at `left: 0%` / `right: 0%` with negative/positive `50%` translations (`translateX(-50%)`/`translateX(50%)`). This shifted the text labels outside the container boundaries, overflowing the viewport and causing horizontal scroll.
- **Tree-View Editor (`PrepTopicManager.jsx`)**: Designed a modern, interactive tree-view manager to administer Categories, Sub Categories, and Topics with smooth toggles and reordering support.
- Adjusted the layout of the pins in [SalarySearch.jsx](file:///d:/job/client/src/pages/SalarySearch.jsx) to align left/right naturally (`textAlign: 'left'` and `textAlign: 'right'`) without translation.
- Added `overflowX: 'hidden'` to the root container of [SalarySearch.jsx](file:///d:/job/client/src/pages/SalarySearch.jsx) as a secondary defense layer to ensure nothing on the page overflows horizontally.
- Added fallback logic that renders the default JavaScript solution if a particular language's solution is missing from the database.
const UserDashboard = React.lazy(() => import('./pages/UserDashboard.jsx'));
- **Problem**: When a category contained many pages of questions (e.g., 57 pages), all page buttons were rendered side-by-side in a single flex row. This caused a massive horizontal overflow that spilled underneath/behind the left sticky sidebar, hiding pages 1 to 34.
- **Layout Exclusion**: Configured `AppLayout` in [App.jsx](file:///d:/job/client/src/App.jsx) to bypass the site header, site footer, pre-footer, and container constraints for the `/admin` path.
- Added a responsive `getPageRange` helper function in [AptitudePrep.jsx](file:///d:/job/client/src/pages/Preparation/AptitudePrep.jsx), [DSAPrep.jsx](file:///d:/job/client/src/pages/Preparation/DSAPrep.jsx), and [TechnicalPrep.jsx](file:///d:/job/client/src/pages/Preparation/TechnicalPrep.jsx).
2. Categories like General Knowledge (which use the `AptitudePrep.jsx` handler) opened by default to a blank formulas tab and displayed an empty exercise selection sidebar (Formulas, DS1, DS2, DS3) that is only relevant for Arithmetic Aptitude.
- Constrained the pagination bar to a clean, fixed width that fits comfortably on all device screens and wraps responsively if needed.
- **Theme States**: Added a dark/light mode toggle with local storage persistence to the admin sidebar/topbar.
- **CSS Variable Injection**: Standardized the admin panel style tokens to use CSS custom variables (`var(--page-bg)`, `var(--card-bg)`, etc.), which swap values automatically.
- **Global Theme Overrides**: Wrote CSS overrides targeting bootstrap classes and inline styling structures to style all nested subcomponents correctly in dark mode.
- Added checks to identify whether the current category is an Aptitude category (`Quantitative Aptitude` or `Aptitude`).
- Non-Aptitude categories (e.g. General Knowledge, Current Affairs, Verbal, Reasoning, etc.) now default directly to the questions view (`'general'`) on mount.
- Conditionally hide the Left Sidebar ("Exercise Selection") for non-Aptitude categories and span the questions grid to `100%` width, establishing visual parity with the other main preparation views.
- Implemented conditional `sticky-prep-header` padding/width and body `maxWidth` constraints (limited to `860px` instead of `1200px` for non-Aptitude categories), giving them the exact same centered, premium, and readable look and feel as the other five preparation pages.
- **Aptitude Category Mapping**: Mapped initial search query categories (`?category=Aptitude`, `?category=Verbal`, `?category=Reasoning`) in [AptitudePrep.jsx](file:///d:/job/client/src/pages/Preparation/AptitudePrep.jsx) to their respective display categories (`Quantitative Aptitude`, `Verbal Ability`, `Logical Reasoning`) so the filter dropdown is correctly selected on page load.
- **Backend Category Filter Mapping**: Updated the `getAptitude` endpoint in [preparationController.js](file:///d:/job/server/controllers/preparationController.js) to query both seeded legacy values (`'Aptitude'`, `'Verbal'`, `'Reasoning'`) and display names (`'Quantitative Aptitude'`, `'Verbal Ability'`, `'Logical Reasoning'`) using a Mongoose `$in` filter.
- **Trigger General Pool Loading**: Fixed a bug where questions were not loaded when a user navigated to `/preparation/aptitude` without a `selectedTopic` parameter. The page now automatically invokes `loadQuestions` and displays the general questions pool matching the query.
- **Problem**: The Technical Preparation page (`/preparation/technical`) previously displayed all coding and interview questions in a single combined list directly on load, lacking a dedicated landing/selection view to browse subcategories (like Java, JavaScript, Python, SQL, etc.) as cards.
